metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-lines-6 = cons "## Cubically receptive: what a process receives" (cons "" (cons "Ceptr, Arthur Brock's work with the MetaCurrency Project, made reception the primitive of computing: a receptor is a unit that receives signals in a protocol it understands and acts on them, and a system is receptors speaking shared protocols, with meaning carried by the protocol rather than by any central authority. Brock set me on my path, and Hyperactive Receptivity formalizes Ceptr's protocols in the language." (cons "" (cons "Cubical type theory gives reception its exact shape. In the cubical model of Cohen, Coquand, Huber and Mörtberg (2015), a type's structure is given by cubes: points, paths between them, squares between paths, and on up. Every cube has faces. An open box is a cube with one face missing; the Kan condition says every open box can be filled, and the filling produces the missing face from the faces present. That is reception made precise: a cubically receptive process receives an open box (the boundary conditions of a situation) and answers with its filling. The whole activity of intelligence is a local, one-step peek at each moment, filling the missing face from the faces adjacent now, and the curvature of a filling, meaning turning as it travels, is content." (cons "" (cons "The cube carries more lineages. Three binary axes give eight corners: the trigrams of the I Ching, the Book of Changes, whose subject is the move from one corner to another along an edge; and the eight directions of each word in dancing in metaphors, a walk through the space of words by binaries on three axes. Six axes give the sixty-four hexagrams Leibniz read as binary numbers, losing the change they encode. And the cube is where Stokes lives: the integral over a region equals the integral over its boundary, so the boundary determines what is inside. I wrote discrete versions of Stokes at fourteen; cubical filling is Stokes made constructive, the inside computed from the boundary." (cons "" nil)))))))
